  "exploratory_before_commit": {
    "note": "Earlier runs of the same probes from uncommitted working trees while the fix was developed; the runner differed from e107d12 only in comments and one unused attribute. Not source-bound.",
    "docker_only_probe": "30 kills: Docker OOMKilled false and no oom event in 6, unchanged 2 s later.",
    "docker_vs_cgroup_probe": "30 kills: Docker missed 4; cgroup oom_kill 1 read in 30 of 30, incl. those 4; count to removal about 10 ms (3-111 ms); cgroup removed before attach returned in 30 of 30.",
    "runner_with_count": "100 memory kills at load averages up to about 90: 97 both sources, 2 cgroup only (Docker missed), 1 Docker only (cgroup read 0, missed); all memory_limit.",
    "runner_count_disabled": "40 memory kills: 3 process_failed with Docker OOMKilled false.",
    "runner_kills": "5 each: deadline_exceeded, cancelled, process_failed (self-SIGKILL), cgroup count 0; a child OOM with exit 0 gave memory_limit with both sources.",
    "pollpri_probe": "4 kills: poll(POLLPRI) woke on the first memory.events change (oom_kill still 0); no later wake arrived for memory.events or cgroup.events before the cgroup was removed."
  },
  "mechanism": [
    "Kernel: mm/oom_kill.c increments the memcg oom_kill event before sending SIGKILL, and only the OOM killer does; cgroup_file_notify limits notifications to one per file per 10 ms and cancels a pending one when the file is removed.",
    "containerd 2.2.1 (code reading, not instrumented): pkg/oom/v2 publishes TaskOOM only from readings of memory.events taken by cgroups/v3 Manager.EventChan on inotify IN_MODIFY of memory.events or cgroup.events. Its forwarding goroutine selects between the event and error channels; after the final reading, EventChan returns and closes the error channel, so that last buffered reading can be dropped.",
    "Docker sets State.OOMKilled only from TaskOOM; when containerd never publishes it, no later inspect can show it."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Local workstation observations, not hosted CI. GitHub ubuntu-24.04 runners also use cgroup v2 with the systemd driver, but their timing differs.",
    "The host read is best effort: the controller thread must run between the count and the cgroup removal (about 10 ms). A run where both Docker and the read miss is still reported process_failed, never guessed.",
    "cgroup_oom_kills is None without a host view of cgroup v2 at /sys/fs/cgroup or with another layout (custom cgroup parent, rootless Docker); classification then uses Docker's flag alone.",
    "No live AOS-008 gate, release gate or R1/G1 evidence is claimed. Historical failures are not relabelled."
  ]
}
